		bodyHtml: `<p>Paul wrote Philippians as a prisoner. Earlier in the letter he says, &ldquo;my chains for Christ became known to the whole imperial guard and everyone else.&rdquo; (Philippians 1:13). The man who writes &ldquo;I can do all things&rdquo; is chained, dependent on gifts from friends, and not in charge of his circumstances. That alone should slow us down before we read the verse as a slogan for winning.</p>`,
