		bodyHtml: `<p>The verse is often printed on trophies and gym walls as a promise that you will succeed at whatever you attempt. Read in its place, it promises something different and, for most people, something more useful. When the job is lost, the diagnosis comes, or the season is hard, Christ gives strength to stay faithful and content there. It is a verse for the valley as much as for the finish line.</p><p>That does not make ambition wrong, and it does not mean prayer for a better situation is wrong. It means this verse should not be used to promise a result our Father has not promised.</p>`,
